  "query_preview": "..Dry conditions are expected across the area through\nat least Thursday, then precipitation chances start to increase. \n\nToday through Thursday...Surface high pressure in place near the\nfour corners will result in northeasterly flow across the area \nwith mild and dry conditions. There is low confidence for any fog\nto occur the next couple nights as lingering moisture in the\nboundary layer becomes limited. A weak trough will cross near or \njust south of southern Arizona on Tuesday, but the system lacks \nstrength and moisture, which means we will likely remain dry \nacross northern Arizona.\n\nFriday through next weekend...Looking towards the end of the \nweek, the models continue to show a deepening west coast trough \nthat becomes a cut-off low as it moves towards Baja California. \nWhile the past few days the models have trended south with the \nlow, the most recent operational runs have shifted the low \nslightly north into southern Arizona. Additionally, they weaken \nthe low as it moves towards the area and then lift it to the \neast/northeast over the weekend. At this point in time confidence\nis moderate for some some showers and gusty winds across the area\nover the weekend, while confidence remains low as to just how \nimpactful this low will be due to its timing, position, and \nstrength. With this being at the very end of the forecast period,\nit bears watching since we have seen a very active pattern across\nthe region and we will need to monitor this to see how the trends\nline up over the next few days.",
